  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Private Infrastructure Development Group core funding contributions financial year 2021-22 - 2024-25</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Private Infrastructure Development Group (PIDG) works to mobilise private sector investment to assist developing countries in developing infrastructure vital to boosting their economic growth and combating poverty. Contributions from Australia through the PIDG Trust support PIDG organisations InfraCo Asia, GuarantCo and the PIDG Technical Assistance facility. InfraCo Asia is a donor funded infrastructure project developer that originates, develops and operates infrastructure assets, focusing on lower income countries. GuarantCo is a company funded by donors that provides local currency guarantees to local / regional banks and bond investors to enable infrastructure projects to raise medium and long-term debt finance. Technical Assistance focuses on ensuring gender mainstreaming, promoting high health and safety standards for infrastructure and benefiting the local environment near projects. The PIDG is a DFAT blended finance mechanism.</narrative>
  </description>
